---
import {cities, nearbyAreas} from '../data/cities';
import type {Scenario} from '../data/cities';
import DealForm from './DealForm.astro';
import {rateStructures,workedExample,dollars} from '../data/loanTerms';
import type {LoanTerms} from '../data/loanTerms';
interface Props { cityName:string; intro:string; angle:string; caution:string; location:string; showCityGrid?:boolean; slug?:string; summaryTerms?:boolean; summarySteps?:boolean; scenario?:Scenario; loanTerms:LoanTerms; }
const {cityName,intro,angle,caution,location,showCityGrid=false,slug,summaryTerms=false,summarySteps=false,scenario,loanTerms}=Astro.props;
const example=workedExample(loanTerms);
const metro = cityName === 'Tucson Metro';
const nearby = slug && nearbyAreas[slug] ? nearbyAreas[slug].map(s=>cities.find(c=>c.slug===s)).filter(Boolean) : [];
---
<section class="hero" id="main"><div class="container hero__inner"><div class="hero__content"><h1>Fix and flip loans <em>{metro ? 'for metro Tucson' : `in ${cityName}, Arizona`}</em></h1><div class="hero__rule"></div><p>{intro}</p><a class="text-link" href="#how-it-works">See how the connection works <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><DealForm cityName={cityName} location={location} /></div></section>
<div class="trust-bar"><div class="container trust-bar__inner"><span>Built around your project</span><span>Asset-based focus</span><span>Clear next steps</span></div></div>
<section class="section" id="local-market"><div class="container split"><div><h2>{metro ? 'A project starts with the property' : `A closer look at ${cityName}`}</h2><p>{angle}</p><p>{caution}</p></div><aside class="side-note"><span class="side-note__mark" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><h3>Start with the actual deal</h3><p>Include the purchase price, scope of work, proposed budget and intended resale. A funding partner can then assess the project on its own merits.</p></aside></div></section>
<section class="section section--tint" id="why-us"><div class="container"><h2>Funding conversations that begin with your plan</h2><p class="section__intro">Asset-based fix and flip funding starts with the property, the proposed improvements and the exit plan rather than relying primarily on personal income. A lender may still review credit, experience and other borrower details. We connect investors with one lending partner rather than making lending decisions ourselves. The <a href="/fix-and-flip-vs-hard-money/">fix and flip vs hard money</a> guide explains how this kind of funding compares to other options.</p><div class="card-grid"><article><span>Property</span><h3>Show what you are buying</h3><p>The address, current condition and contract details give a funding partner a starting point. Include what you know and flag what is still being checked.</p></article><article><span>Renovation</span><h3>Explain the work</h3><p>Share the repair scope and budget you have prepared. If inspections may change the plan, say so up front.</p></article><article><span>Exit</span><h3>Make the resale case</h3><p>Nearby comparable sales and your intended buyer help explain the project. No one can guarantee a resale price or an approval.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="sample-terms"><div class="container"><h2>Fix and flip financing structures</h2><p class="section__intro">Our program lists financing up to {loanTerms.fundingMax}, {loanTerms.closingSpeed} and {loanTerms.drawTiming}. Our listed terms are {loanTerms.feeDisclosure}. Review the complete written offer for your property, including any closing or draw costs. These are our listed program terms, not approval or a guarantee of financing, closing speed or draw timing.</p><div class="compare-wrap"><table class="compare-table structure-table"><caption class="sr-only">Our two listed fix and flip financing structures</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Term</th>{rateStructures(loanTerms).map(structure => <th scope="col">{structure.name}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">At closing</th>{rateStructures(loanTerms).map(structure => <td>{structure.closing}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Monthly payment</th>{rateStructures(loanTerms).map(structure => <td>{structure.monthly} payments</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Balloon</th>{rateStructures(loanTerms).map(structure => <td>{structure.balloon}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Optional extension</th>{rateStructures(loanTerms).map(structure => <td>{loanTerms.extensionMonths} for {structure.extension}, only if all payments have been made on time</td>)}</tr></tbody></table></div><p class="term-disclosure">Our lending partner serves Arizona. Eligibility, final costs and timing depend on its review and written loan documents. See <a href="/fix-and-flip-loan-costs/">how to compare loan costs</a>.</p></div></section>
{slug === 'tucson' && example && <section class="section section--tint" id="worked-deal"><div class="container"><h2>How a Tucson flip loan could work</h2><p class="section__intro">Illustrative {dollars(example.amount)} loan held for {example.months} months, with {example.assumption.toLowerCase()}. The loan amount and hold period are editable sample inputs in our program terms sheet; the figures below are calculated from that sheet's current rates and points.</p><div class="compare-wrap"><table class="compare-table structure-table"><caption>Illustrative financing cost, excluding principal and other charges</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Cost</th>{example.structures.map(x=><th scope="col">{x.name}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Closing points</th>{example.structures.map(x=><td>{dollars(x.points)}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Monthly interest</th>{example.structures.map(x=><td>{dollars(x.monthly)}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Interest for {example.months} months</th>{example.structures.map(x=><td>{dollars(x.interest)}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Points + interest</th>{example.structures.map(x=><td>{dollars(x.total)}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Optional extension points, if eligible</th>{example.structures.map(x=><td>{dollars(x.extension)}</td>)}</tr></tbody></table></div><p class="term-disclosure">This simplified example assumes the full loan balance is outstanding for the hold period. It excludes repayment of principal, closing and title charges, insurance, draw or inspection fees, taxes and any other costs in an actual offer. An extension is not automatic and requires on-time payments. Our lending partner determines eligibility and gives the final terms in writing; no funding, timing or profit is guaranteed.</p></div></section>}
{summarySteps ? (
<section class="section section--dark" id="how-it-works"><div class="container"><h2>How the connection works</h2><p class="section__intro">The process is the same in every city we serve: send the project, discuss the details, then review any terms a lender offers. The full sequence and the paperwork behind it are in our guide to <a href="/how-fix-and-flip-funding-works-in-arizona/">how fix and flip funding works in Arizona</a>, and the <a href="/fix-and-flip-vs-hard-money/">fix and flip vs hard money</a> guide explains how this kind of funding compares.</p></div></section>
) : (
<section class="section section--dark" id="how-it-works"><div class="container"><h2>How the connection works</h2><p class="section__intro">The steps below stay the same in every city we serve. The full process, the paperwork a file usually needs and the questions worth asking are in our guide to <a href="/how-fix-and-flip-funding-works-in-arizona/">how fix and flip funding works in Arizona</a>.</p><div class="step-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Send the project</h3><p>Tell us about the property, your proposed purchase and the work you plan to do. You can identify anything that still needs confirmation.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Discuss the details</h3><p>We review the information and may ask for more context. That helps identify whether a funding partner might be a fit for the deal.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Review available terms</h3><p>Our lending partner decides eligibility, terms and documentation. Review the full offer and costs before deciding whether to move forward.</p></article></div></div></section>
)}
{scenario && <section class="section scenario" id="local-example"><div class="container"><h2>{scenario.title}</h2><p class="section__intro">{scenario.intro}</p><ol class="scenario__list">{scenario.items.map(item=><li>{item}</li>)}</ol><p class="scenario__outro" set:html={scenario.outro}/></div></section>}
<section class="section section--tint" id="faq"><div class="container faq"><h2>Questions before you submit</h2><div><details><summary>Are you our lending partner?</summary><p>No. Tucson Fix & Flip Loan connects investors with one lending partner. Our lending partner makes its own decisions and provides the actual terms.</p></details><details><summary>What should I include about the project?</summary><p>Start with the property address, purchase details, renovation plan, budget and intended resale. If a detail is still unknown, explain what you are checking.</p></details><details><summary>What rates or loan amounts are available?</summary><p>The two structures above are our listed program terms, not a loan offer. Our lending partner decides eligibility and final terms for each property. Review its written offer before deciding.</p></details><details><summary>Does submitting a deal guarantee funding?</summary><p>No. A submission starts a review and possible introduction. It does not guarantee a match, approval or a particular outcome.</p></details></div></div></section>
{showCityGrid && <section class="section section--tint" id="service-areas"><div class="container"><h2>Explore metro Tucson</h2><p class="section__intro">Every property deserves a local look. Find your city below, then share the details of your project.</p><div class="city-grid">{cities.map(c=><a href={`/${c.slug}/`}><span>{c.county} County</span><strong>{c.name}</strong><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>)}</div></div></section>}
{nearby.length>0 && <section class="nearby" aria-label="Nearby service areas"><div class="container"><h2 class="nearby__title">Nearby service areas</h2><ul class="nearby__list">{nearby.map(c=><li><a href={`/${c.slug}/`}>{c.name}, AZ</a></li>)}</ul></div></section>}
<section class="final-cta"><div class="container"><h2>Have a property in mind?</h2><p>Tell us what you plan to buy and improve. We will review the details and discuss possible funding connections without promising a loan.</p><a class="btn" href="#deal-form">Submit your project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
<style>
.structure-table{table-layout:fixed;width:100%}
.structure-table th,.structure-table td{overflow-wrap:anywhere}
.structure-table thead th:first-child,.structure-table tbody th{width:28%}
@media(max-width:600px){.structure-table{font-size:12px}.structure-table.compare-table thead th,.structure-table.compare-table tbody th,.structure-table.compare-table td{padding:9px 7px;white-space:normal}.structure-table thead th:first-child,.structure-table tbody th{width:28%}}
</style>
